{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/900197-question-about-scotland-attire","id":900197,"title":"Question about Scotland Attire","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-26T11:14:53-07:00","id":900197,"title":"Question about Scotland Attire","content":"Due to Touken Ranbu, drawing personification of historical swords is all the rage right now with some of the female (and sometime, male) in my country. I promised with my friend to draw the sword of William Wallace, but I'm stuck at the design phase right now. So I'm hoping that Scottish forumite or those who have knowledge about Scotland culture can help me out with this.<br /> <br /> I have three choices for his design right now:<br /> <br /> 1/ Medieval knight attire like his master, but after some Google search I can't quite find the differences between a Scottish knight and a generic European knight.......Do you have any suggestions to make people go &quot;Ah, that's a Scottish knight~&quot;, I guuuess I can go with the stereotype of barbarian in tartan kilt + facepaint, but I'm allergic to historical inaccuracies in clothing.<br /> <br /> 2/ Full on fantasy Scottish attire, except I have no idea what it would look like aside from the stereotype mentioned in 1.<br /> <br /> 3/ Modern cloth. Is this what Scottish men wear ?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.1st-art-gallery.com/thumbnail/226014/1/Two-Men-In-Highland-Dress.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Also, are Scottish men....:look sideway:.....hairy.....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 05-26-2016, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T11:53:55-07:00","id":900230,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Kilts weren't invented for several hundred years after Wallace. What do you mean by &quot;drawing personification of historical swords?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T12:11:50-07:00","id":900241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/900197-question-about-scotland-attire?p=900230#post900230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by &quot;drawing personification of historical swords?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The main character of the game has the ability to bring inanimate objects to life\u2014in this case, historically famous swords, all of which take on the forms of handsome men. Basically, every sword has a spirit and you can make a physical body for them to wield their...eh....themself...<br /> <br /> The original game is about Japanese swords, but the fans are drawing pictures of pretty much every swords in every countries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T00:51:23-07:00","id":905452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/900197-question-about-scotland-attire#post900197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1/ Medieval knight attire like his master, but after some Google search I can't quite find the differences between a Scottish knight and a generic European knight.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the time, no real difference visually. However, at the time the English (and I am told the Scottish) men-at-arms normally fought on foot instead of on horse. This changes the armor in some fairly drastic ways. <a href=\"https://youtu.be/5tgLeMS30j8\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/5tgLeMS30j8</a> (the armor they are talking about is about a century later but is should give you some ideas.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/900197-question-about-scotland-attire#post900197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, are Scottish men....:look sideway:.....hairy.....</div> </div> </div> </div>Fortunatly no. However, there was normally a cultural stigma about not having a beard. The &quot;unbearded youth&quot; idea. At the time, it would probably mean about the same as calling someone a virgin now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T22:00:27-07:00","id":906207,"title":"","content":"I still can't believe the person who asked me to draw this is a girl :'O<br /> <br /> And concept designing is hard as hell, I rolled around on the floor for two days and the only thing Scottish about him is the kilt :ashamed:<img src=\"http://i.imgbox.com/RA1YP7KJ.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}